      en: "A major sports stadium in Tamale, newly built for the 2008 Africa Cup of Nations. Seats 21,017 spectators. Named after a former Vice President. Home of Real Tamale United. Multipurpose facility. Thus, the site is among the characteristic points of Ghana — a country shaped by its Atlantic coastline, the Volta river system, the legacy of the Ashanti Kingdom, and its cocoa and gold wealth — and offers insight into the regional identity. Located in the West African state of Ghana along the Gulf of Guinea coast."
