      en: "A majestic church in Cape Coast that played a central role in the spread of Methodism in Ghana. Built in 1838. Considered the mother church of Methodists in Ghana. Expanded multiple times. A striking architectural work. Thus, the site is among the characteristic points of Ghana — a country shaped by its Atlantic coastline, the Volta river system, the legacy of the Ashanti Kingdom, and its cocoa and gold wealth — and offers insight into the regional identity. Located in the West African state of Ghana along the Gulf of Guinea coast."
