      en: "A former Portuguese fort in Axim, the second oldest structure of its kind on the coast of Ghana. Construction began in 1515. Later captured by the Dutch. Served the gold trade for a long time. Part of UNESCO World Heritage. Thus, the site is among the characteristic points of Ghana — a country shaped by its Atlantic coastline, the Volta river system, the legacy of the Ashanti Kingdom, and its cocoa and gold wealth — and offers insight into the regional identity."
