      en: "The Jamestown Colonial Building in Accra is a historic 19th-century building. It originally served as the residence of the British governor. The building is in the Georgian style with a distinctive façade featuring columns and balconies. It is located in Jamestown, one of Accra's oldest neighborhoods. After independence, it housed various government agencies. Today it is a museum showcasing Ghana's colonial history. The building is surrounded by a wall and has an inner courtyard. It is a popular destination for tourists and photographers. Restoration took place in 2005. It is a symbol of Ghana's colonial past.",
